The '''Volkswagen Golf (Mk7)''' is a [[C-segment]] car manufactured by German automobile manufacturer [[Volkswagen]]. It is the seventh generation in the [[Volkswagen Golf|Golf]] series and the successor to the [[Volkswagen Golf Mk6|Golf Mk6]], and was introduced in [[Berlin]] on 4 September 2012, before a public launch at the [[2012 Paris Motor Show]],<ref>{{cite web |last=Kable |first=Greg |date=4 September 2012 |title=2013 Volkswagen Golf revealed |url=http://www.autocar.co.uk/car-news/2013-volkswagen-golf/2013-volkswagen-golf-revealed |access-date=4 September 2012 |work=[[Autocar (magazine)|Autocar]]}}</ref> with European sales beginning in November 2012 for the 2013 model year.<ref>{{cite web |language=de |url=http://www.auto-motor-und-sport.de/news/vw-golf-vii-markteinfuehrung-am-samstag-6054109.html |title=VW Golf VII: Markteinführung am Samstag |trans-title=VW Golf VII: Going on sale Saturday |website=Auto, Motor und Sport |date=7 November 2012 | access-date=14 July 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150715023847/http://www.auto-motor-und-sport.de/news/vw-golf-vii-markteinfuehrung-am-samstag-6054109.html |archive-date=15 July 2015}}</ref>

Marketed in three-door and five-door [[hatchback]], [[van]], and [[station wagon|estate]] forms, the Golf Mk7 shares the [[Volkswagen Group MQB platform|MQB platform]] with the third generation [[Audi A3]], [[SEAT León]] and [[Škoda Octavia]].

In November 2016, Volkswagen presented a [[Facelift (automotive)|facelift]] of the Golf Mk7.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.faz.net/1.4521530 |title=Weltpremiere in Wolfsburg: VW hat den Golf renoviert |first=Frankfurter Allgemeine Zeitung |last=GmbH |date=10 November 2016 |newspaper=FAZ.NET}}</ref> It was replaced in December 2019 by the [[Volkswagen Golf Mk8|Golf Mk8]], which is built on the [[Volkswagen Group MQB platform#MQB Evo (2019)|MQB Evo]] platform.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.thedrive.com/news/30141/2020-volkswagen-golf-mk8-set-for-october-24-debut-in-wolfsburg-report |title=2020 Volkswagen Golf MK8 Set for October 24 Debut in Wolfsburg: Report |website=The Drive |last=Gilboy |first=James |date=3 October 2019}}</ref> Production of the e-Golf and the Golf Variant ended in mid-2020.<ref name="16.155 e-Golf">{{Cite web |url=https://www.glaesernemanufaktur.de/de/news-ergebnisseite/16.155-eGolf.html |title=VW Gläserne Manufaktur - 16.155 e-Golf: Gläserne Manufaktur 2019 mit Allzeit-Produktionsrekord |website=VW Gläserne Manufaktur |language=de |access-date=22 January 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.volkswagen-newsroom.com:443/de/pressemitteilungen/produktion-des-id3-im-werk-zwickau-startet-im-november-5322 |title=Produktion des ID.3 im Werk Zwickau startet im November |website=Volkswagen Newsroom |language=de |access-date=22 January 2020 }}{{Dead link|date=August 2025 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref>


